  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 日本語版「ヌルデ」",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%83%8C%E3%83%AB%E3%83%87",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 110855185,
      "text": "ヌルデ は、ウルシ科ヌルデ属の落葉小高木。山野の林縁などに生える。ウルシほどではないが、まれにかぶれる人もいる。別名フシノキ、カチノキ（カツノキ）。葉にできた虫えいを五倍子（ごばいし／ふし）という。お歯黒の材料にしたり、材は細工物や護摩を焚くのに使われる。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Rhus chinensis」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rhus_chinensis",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1322974701,
      "text": "Rhus chinensis, the Chinese sumac or nutgall tree, is a deciduous shrub or small tree in the genus Rhus. Growing to 6 m (20 ft) tall, it has downy shoots and leaves comprising several leaflets. These turn red in autumn before falling."
    }
